The palatal approximant {{IPAblink|j}} also occurs in Retta (and Blagar) but is analyzed as an [[allophone]] of the vowel {{IPAslink|i}} rather than a separate [[phoneme]]. {{IPAslink|s}} occurs mostly in [[loanword]]s or other non-native words.<ref name=Willemsen2020/>{{rp|190-191}}

===Vowels===
Retta has eight single vowels ([[monophthong]]s), which differ in length, height, and backness. Three are always [[Vowel length|long vowels]] ({{IPA|eː}} {{IPA|oː}} {{IPA|aː}}), two are always short vowels ({{IPA|ɛ}} {{IPA|ɔ}}), and the remaining three are short in most contexts but can be made long via phonological processes.<ref name=Willemsen2020/>{{rp|193}}

